# LearnCraft Architecture Overhaul — Implementation Plan

Based on the [Architecture Analysis](file:///C:/Users/Mehedi%20Hasan/.gemini/antigravity-ide/brain/c7bba08d-d277-40be-95cd-9ddf8ee5b19d/learncraft_architecture_analysis.md), this plan transforms LearnCraft from a "look how much content we have" platform into a "here is your clear next step" experience.

---

## What This Plan Changes (Big Picture)

```mermaid
graph LR
    A["Current: 32 lessons dumped<br/>on one page"] --> B["New: Focused journey<br/>showing one step at a time"]
    C["Current: 17 locked sidebar<br/>steps per lesson"] --> D["New: 4-6 unlocked<br/>concept sections"]
    E["Current: '12/32 complete'<br/>progress"] --> F["New: 'You can now<br/>build a REST API'<br/>milestones"]
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **No educational content is removed.** Every existing explanation, exercise, and project is preserved. This plan changes *how* content is presented, not *what* content exists. All lesson text and code examples will also follow a **plain-language, easy-words standard** — simple sentences, real-world analogies, and beginner-friendly code comments.

---

## Scope & Constraints

- **Framework**: Next.js 16 (App Router), React 18, Tailwind CSS 3.4
- **State**: localStorage for progress (no backend yet)
- **Built lessons**: NJ-01 (flat scroll layout), NJ-02/03/04 (stepper-sidebar pattern)
- **Existing registries**: [`topic-registry.ts`](file:///f:/My%20Projects/LearnCraft/lib/topic-registry.ts) — lesson metadata for NestJS, Next.js, TanStack Query

