### Component 1: Curriculum Data Layer

**Problem it solves:** Right now, all lesson data (names, descriptions, phase assignments, theme colors) is hardcoded inside [`app/learn/nestjs/page.tsx`](file:///f:/My%20Projects/LearnCraft/app/learn/nestjs/page.tsx#L37-L408) as a 370-line `PHASES` constant. Other files like [`topic-registry.ts`](file:///f:/My%20Projects/LearnCraft/lib/topic-registry.ts) maintain a *separate* copy of lesson names and paths. These two sources already disagree (e.g., the registry says `nj11-pipes` but the filesystem has `nj11-request-lifecycle`).

**What we build:** One shared file that every other component reads from.

#### [NEW] `lib/curriculum.ts`

**Types it defines:**

```typescript
