### Component 2: Progress & Milestone Engine

**Problem it solves:** Currently, each lesson stores its own progress under a separate localStorage key (e.g., `learncraft_progress_nj02-oop-foundations`). There is no cross-lesson awareness — the landing page doesn't know which lessons are complete, and no milestones are tracked.

#### [NEW] `lib/progress.ts`

**Stores one object per learning path:**

```typescript
export interface PathProgress {
  pathId: string;
  goal: LearnerGoal | null;                     // what the learner chose
  completedLessons: string[];                    // ["nj01-typescript-essentials", ...]
  completedStages: string[];                     // ["build-foundation", ...]
  skippedLessons: string[];                      // "I already know this"
  currentLessonSlug: string | null;              // where they left off
  lessonSectionProgress: Record<string, string[]>; // per-lesson section tracking
}
```

**localStorage key:** `learncraft_path_nestjs` (one key per path, not per lesson)

**Functions:**
- `getProgress(pathId)` — read current state
- `markLessonComplete(pathId, slug)` — mark done, auto-detect stage completion
- `markLessonSkipped(pathId, slug)` — "I already know this"
- `setGoal(pathId, goal)` — store selected goal
- `getCurrentMilestone(pathId)` — last completed stage's milestone
- `getNextMilestone(pathId)` — what the learner is working toward
- `migrateLegacyProgress()` — detect old `learncraft_progress_nj*` keys, merge into new format, delete old keys

#### [NEW] `context/progress-context.tsx`

React context + `useProgress(pathId)` hook so all components can read/write progress without prop-drilling. Wraps the layout so it's available everywhere inside `/learn/nestjs/`.

