### Component 4: Unified Lesson Shell

**Problem it solves:** Currently, every lesson page duplicates ~200 lines of sidebar/stepper/progress code. NJ-02 has 17 locked steps, NJ-03 has 21 locked steps, NJ-04 has 15. The sidebar labels teaching tools ("Beginner Mistakes", "Concept Tables") as equal-weight curriculum items. All steps after the current one are hard-locked.

#### [NEW] `app/learn/nestjs/components/lesson-shell.tsx`

**A reusable wrapper that every lesson uses:**

```tsx
interface LessonSection {
  id: string;
  label: string;
  type: 'concept' | 'practice' | 'summary';
  component: React.ComponentType;
}

interface LessonShellProps {
  pathId: string;
  lessonSlug: string;
  title: string;
  goals: string[];       // "What you will understand"
  abilities: string[];   // "What you will be able to do"
  sections: LessonSection[];
}
```

**Key changes from the current stepper:**

| What | Current | New |
|---|---|---|
| Sidebar header | "Modules" | "Sections" |
| Visible steps | 15–21 | 3–6 concepts + Practice + Summary |
| Locking | Hard-locked (can't click ahead) | All sections freely clickable |
| Teaching tools | Separate sidebar entries | Collapsible inside concept sections |
| Progress label | "{n} of {total} modules" | Simple progress bar, no label |
| Lesson header | None | "What you will understand" + "What you will build" |
| End of lesson | Nothing | Skill statement + next lesson card + Continue button |
| Breadcrumb | None | Learn NestJS → Stage Name → Lesson Name |

**The lesson shell provides:**
- Breadcrumb navigation
- Lesson header with goals and abilities
- Unlocked sidebar with 3–6 sections
- Progress bar (within this lesson only)
- "Previous lesson" / "Next lesson" navigation (reads from `curriculum.ts`)
- Lesson-complete celebration with milestone text

