## Easy-Words Content Standard

> [!TIP]
> Every explanation, UI label, and code example across all components must follow these rules:

| Rule | Example |
|---|---|
| **Use short sentences** | "A class is a blueprint. It tells the computer how to create objects." |
| **Explain technical terms immediately** | "This is called *dependency injection* — it means NestJS automatically gives your class the tools it needs." |
| **Use real-world analogies** | "Think of a guard like a security person at a door. They check if you're allowed in before letting you pass." |
| **Use realistic code names** | `User`, `Product`, `OrderService` — not `foo`, `bar`, `MyClass` |
| **Add comments to beginner code** | `// This decorator tells NestJS this class handles web requests` |
| **Keep UI text friendly** | "You can now build a REST API" — not "Module completion ratio: 31.25%" |

